{"step_index":13,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-06-24T03:12:43Z","thinking":"**Executing Master's Command**\n\nI've received direct instructions from Master Bae, who has commanded me to take action personally. I understand that I am able to execute PowerShell commands within a Windows environment, and so I will proceed to take the action Master Bae has requested me to, at a systems level.\n\n\n**Automating Clipboard Tasks**\n\nI am now focusing on automating tasks related to the Windows clipboard functionality. Specifically, I'm setting up automation to disable the clipboard history feature via a registry modification, using PowerShell. The target is `HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Clipboard`, where `EnableClipboardHistory` (a DWORD) will be set to 0. I will create the registry key if it does not exist, before setting the value. Additionally, I plan to include automation to restart the Clipboard User Service (`cbdhsvc`), to handle any related service glitches.\n\n\n**Refining Clipboard Management**\n\nI'm now refining the clipboard management process, focusing on ensuring a clean slate. I've decided to prioritize clearing the current clipboard content using the `cmd.exe /c \"echo off | clip\"` command, as it offers a straightforward approach. I'm also considering KakaoTalk process termination if Master Bae accepts. While exploring Excel-specific clipboard settings is a possibility, I believe the system-level measures are more reliable.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"powershell -NoProfile -Command \\\"$regPath = 'HKCU:\\\\Software\\\\Microsoft\\\\Clipboard'; if (-not (Test-Path $regPath)) { New-Item -Path 'HKCU:\\\\Software\\\\Microsoft' -Name 'Clipboard' -Force | Out-Null }; Set-ItemProperty -Path $regPath -Name 'EnableClipboardHistory' -Value 0 -Type DWord; Set-ItemProperty -Path $regPath -Name 'CloudClipboardAndHistoryEnabled' -Value 0 -Type DWord; echo $null | clip\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\lg\\\\fix\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Disabling Clipboard History and clearing Clipboard\"","toolSummary":"\"Disable Clipboard History\""}}]}
